	The classic form of the experiment has a cat in a close box, a
closed jar of prussic acid, and a mechinism to shatter the jar dependant
on whether or not a *single* radioactive atom decayed.

	Since the box is sealed and the atom has, at any instant, a
50-50 chance of decaying, the cat should be *both* alive and dead until
the box is opened and one result or the other is measured to be true.

	So you should be able to get a live cat out of the box.

